{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12459 - MONDO_16248",
  "verbalization": "Belotecan is associated with Familial Ovarian Cancer through a chain of indications involving Altretamine, which is linked to the same condition. The evidence suggests that Belotecan may be repurposed for treating malignancies of the ovary, including Granulosa Cell Tumor and Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor, both of which are classified under the broader category of Familial Ovarian Cancer. The shared indication with Altretamine, a known chemotherapy agent, implies a potential mechanism of action that could be relevant to the development or treatment of this cancer. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Belotecan to Familial Ovarian Cancer highlights the possibility of a shared biological pathway or therapeutic mechanism, though the exact relationship remains to be elucidated.",
